# P3-2 Task 6 (R7): -implicit_functors OWA fixture pair, "unknown functor"
# half. Byte-identical to implicit_functors_unknown_plain.clausal except for
# the directive line -- driven by TestImplicitFunctors in
# tests/test_implicit_functors.py. Under OWA a keyword-free construction of
# an UNDECLARED functor (no ``-module`` signature at all) is advisory: it
# compiles to a cell instead of a runtime ``NameError``.  The unflagged twin
# pins today's default (checked) behaviour on the identical construct.
-implicit_functors
-module(implicit_functors_unknown_owa, [
    p(A),
    unwrap(W, X, Y),
])

# ``wibble`` has no signature anywhere in this module -- under OWA that is
# still a legal keyword-free construction, at whatever arity is written.
p(wibble(1, 2)),

# Head-side symmetry (the phase's standing principle): the SAME OWA-unknown
# functor pattern-matches in a clause HEAD, not just at construction.
unwrap(wibble(X, Y), X, Y),
